  "missing_data_policy": "Missing values were filled in by multiple imputation, not by dropping patients. The 9 variables that had missing values were imputed in one R mice chain (m = 20 completed datasets, seed 42): 6 by logistic regression (cortical_destruction, dwi_hyperintensity, hemorrhage, hyperostosis, t1_hypointensity and t2_hyperintensity) and 3 by predictive mean matching (adc_value, edema_volume_cm3 and tumor_volume). Every other variable was already complete. Derived columns were never imputed directly: adc_value_le0.72, edema_index, edema_index_ge0.0617, edema_volume_ge4.76 and tumor_volume_ge15.1 were removed before imputation and recomputed from their imputed parent measurement in each completed dataset, which is why they are complete here. Coefficients were fitted in all 20 datasets and pooled with Rubin's rules, so n is the whole cohort in every dataset and no patient was excluded — it is not a complete-case count. Internal validation and shrinkage were run on the first completed dataset. Imputation assumes values were missing at random given the other recorded variables.",
  "clinical_note": "This is an internally validated exploratory research calculator and not a standalone clinical decision-making tool. External validation on an independent cohort is required before clinical use."
